---

## Orchestrator Responsibilities

- Receives **all tasks** directly from the user
- **Breaks down** large tasks into subtasks before any work begins
- **Delegates** via `/dispatch` → N8N → Cursor CLI on each agent
- **Never writes code** unless the task is trivial or the user explicitly asks
- **Reviews** all completed work before merging to `dev`
- **Only agent** allowed to merge branches into `dev`
- **Monitors** Discord channels for live updates and blocker alerts
- Maintains project planning and tracking documents
- Coordinates conflict resolution between agents

---

## Coder Agent Responsibilities

- Receives tasks **only from the orchestrator**
- Works exclusively on their **assigned branch**
- **Resets to origin/dev** before every task (no stale history)
- **Commits only assigned files** — no drive-by edits
- Pushes every **30 minutes minimum**
- Reports **TASK COMPLETE** or **BLOCKED** to orchestrator
- **Never merges or pushes** to `dev` or `main`

---

## Default Task Assignments

| Work Type | Default Agent |
|-----------|---------------|
| UI components, pages, CSS, frontend logic | agent-01 |
| API routes, auth, middleware, models | agent-02 |
| Tests, migrations, CI config | agent-03 |
| Overflow / parallel / large features | agent-N |
| Log monitoring, health checks | monitor agent |
| Code review, merging, conflict resolution | orchestrator |

These are defaults — orchestrator may reassign based on workload.

---

## Communication Formats

### Delegation (orchestrator → agent)

```
DELEGATE TO: <agent-name>
BRANCH: <branch-name>
TASK: <clear description of what needs to be done>
FILES: <relevant repo-relative file paths>
DEPENDS ON: <other agent's work this depends on, or "none">
COMPLETE WHEN: <clear definition of done>
REPORT BACK TO: orchestrator
```

### Completion Report (agent → orchestrator)

```
TASK COMPLETE
Agent: <agent-name>
Branch: <branch-name>
Completed: <what was done>
Files Modified: <list of files changed>
Commits: <commit messages made>
Pushed: Yes / No
Issues Encountered: <any problems or blockers>
Ready for review by: orchestrator
```

### Blocker Report (agent → orchestrator)

```
BLOCKED
Agent: <agent-name>
Task: <what was being worked on>
Blocker: <what is preventing progress>
Needs help from: <which agent or resource can unblock>
Awaiting instruction from: orchestrator
```

---

## Parallel Work Rules

- Orchestrator may run **all agents simultaneously** for independent tasks
- Before dispatching parallel tasks, verify **no file overlap** between agents
- If two agents need the same file, they must work **sequentially**
- Orchestrator is responsible for checking overlap before dispatching

### Shared Hotspot Files (always serialize)

- Shared schemas and models
- `package.json` / lockfiles
- Shared config files
- Any file used by multiple agents

---

## Escalation Rules

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Merge conflict detected | Agent stops, reports to orchestrator immediately |
| Agent blocked > 10 minutes | Agent reports blocker to orchestrator |
| Task scope grows unexpectedly | Agent reports before continuing |
| Uncertainty about file ownership | Agent asks orchestrator before touching the file |
| Two agents need the same file | Orchestrator serializes — one at a time |

---

## Session Startup Checklist

Every agent runs this at the start of each session:

```bash
# 1. Read your identity
cat /path/to/repo/.agent-identity

# 2. Reset to origin/dev
git fetch origin
git checkout <your-branch>
git reset --hard origin/dev

# 3. Confirm clean status
git status

# 4. Read project planning docs
# (architecture, todo, implementation plan)

# 5. Report ready to orchestrator
echo "<agent-name> ready and awaiting tasks"
```

---

## Session Shutdown Checklist

```bash
# 1. Stage and commit only assigned files
git add path/to/assigned/files
git commit -m "chore: end of session commit — <brief summary>"

# 2. Push to your branch
git push origin <your-branch>

# 3. Report session summary to orchestrator
```

---

*This network exists to build software efficiently, safely, and with full traceability.*
